#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# coefficient_arrays

#% text
# `coefficient_arrays(polys, vars)` gives the list `[a0, a1, ..., ad]` of arrays of the coefficients of the polynomial, or list of polynomials, in the variables `vars`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `a0` holds the constant terms, `a1` the linear coefficients (one row per polynomial), `a2` the quadratic ones at the positions `[i, j]` with `i <= j`, and so on.

#% item
# For a list of `m` polynomials every array has a leading dimension `m`; for a single polynomial it has none.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
coefficient_arrays(x^2 + x*y + 3 + 2*y, [x, y])
#% output
#= [3, [0, 2], [[1, 1], [0, 0]]]

#% cell
coefficient_arrays([x + 2*y - 1, 3*x*y], [x, y])
#% output
#= [[-1, 0], [[1, 2], [0, 0]], [[[0, 0], [0, 0]], [[0, 3], [0, 0]]]]

#% cell
coefficient_arrays(5*x^3, [x])
#% output
#= [0, [0], [[0]], [[[5]]]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `coefficient_rules`, `coefficient_list`, `coefficient`
